explicit rule $u_n = 7n - 4$ $(n \\ge 1)$? [2]","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Which recursive definition **generates** the sequence with explicit rule "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"u_n = 7n - 4"}},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"(n \\ge 1)"}},{"type":"text","text":"? [2]"}]}]},"e":"$u_1 = 7(1)-4 = 3$ and the constant difference is 7.","m":2,"df":"medium","tp":"Recursive definitions","st":"explicit to recursive","cfg":{"question_number":26,"paper_question_key":26,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"C","criterion_label":"Criterion C — Communicating","criterion_title":"Communicating","difficulty_level":"intermediate","marks":2,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"permitted","assessment_style":"myp_summative","source":"myp5-grade10-sequences-version-c-2026-27"}},{"n":27,"t":"assess_parts","p":"**Rewrite** $u_n = 12\\left(\\frac12\\right)^{n-1}$ $(n \\ge 1)$ as a recursive rule: [2]\n$u_1 =$ ______ , $u_{n+1} =$ ______ $(n \\ge 1)$","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Rewrite** "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"u_n = 12\\left(\\frac12\\right)^{n-1}"}},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"(n \\ge 1)"}},{"type":"text","text":" as a recursive rule: [2]"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"u_1 ="}},{"type":"text","text":" ______ , "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"u_{n+1} ="}},{"type":"text","text":" ______ "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"(n \\ge 1)"}}]}]},"e":"$u_1 = 12$ and each term is half the previous term, so $u_{n+1} = \\frac12 u_n$.","m":2,"df":"medium","tp":"Recursive definitions","st":"explicit to recursive","cfg":{"question_number":27,"paper_question_key":27,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"C","criterion_label":"Criterion C — Communicating","criterion_title":"Communicating","difficulty_level":"intermediate","marks":2,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"permitted","assessment_style":"myp_summative","marking_breakdown":[{"label":"Initial term","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"Recursive rule","marks":1,"focus":""}],"parts":[{"id":"u1","label":"u1","prompt":"Initial term","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what u1 is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for u1."],"answer":12,"tolerance":0},{"id":"rule","label":"un+1","prompt":"Recursive rule in terms of u_n","kind":"expression","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what un+1 is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for un+1."],"accepted":["(1/2)u_n","1/2*u_n","0.5u_n","u_n/2","1/2 u_n","0.5*u_n"]}],"source":"myp5-grade10-sequences-version-c-2026-27"}},{"n":28,"t":"assess_parts","p":"A Porto-Novo cooperative weaves 56 baskets in Month 1 (+8 baskets/month). [3]\n**(i) Month 10: $u_{10} =$** ______   **(ii) Months for $S_n = 792$: $n =$** ______","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A Porto-Novo cooperative weaves 56 baskets in Month 1 (+8 baskets/month). [3]"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**(i) Month 10: "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"u_{10} ="}},{"type":"text","text":"** ______   **(ii) Months for "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"S_n = 792"}},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"n ="}},{"type":"text","text":"** ______"}]}]},"e":"$u_{10} = 56 + 9(8) = 128$. $S_n = \\frac n2[112+8(n-1)] = 4n^2+52n = 792$, so $n^2+13n-198=(n-9)(n+22)=0$ and $n=9$ months.","m":3,"df":"hard","tp":"Arithmetic applications","st":"basket production","cfg":{"question_number":28,"paper_question_key":28,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"D","criterion_label":"Criterion D — Applying mathematics in real-life contexts","criterion_title":"Applying mathematics in real-life contexts","difficulty_level":"advanced","marks":3,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"permitted","assessment_